# ::tok Despite this, the stubbornness of the wage growth rate is difficult to reverse the current trend of rapid decline in inflation. With the year-on-year negative M2 data and the gradual improvement of leading indicators in various CPI segments, the US CPI data has moved to a stage of rapid decline since October. The stubbornness of the wage growth rate will only underpin future inflation data. Current market expectations are difficult to falsify, and the market may enter a new round of the game after the next inflation data is released.
