# ::tok I personally think it's also acceptable. First, the price is cheap, and the 700-plus pages are split into two, making it easy to read as a paperback book; secondly, unlike the Michelangelo Complete Collection, paintings are the main body; Leonardo da Vinci's black and white manuscript accounts for most of the time. For readers with limited budgets and non-art professionals, this edition is the most cost-effective for readers who appreciate paintings and manuscripts.
